# This package is consumed as a *named build context* by the applications that vendor the workspace
# UI:
#
#   docker build --build-context taxpert=../taxpert/packages/ui …
#
# and a named context has no .dockerignore of its own to fall back on — the application's
# .dockerignore applies only to the application's own context. Without this file, a developer's
# `node_modules/` rides along into every image build that names this directory.
#
# Those builds copy `src`, plus `scripts/` and the manifests they need to build the bundle in a
# Node stage of their own, but the whole directory is still transferred first.
#
# `dist/` is excluded deliberately. It is the bundle, and an image must build its own from the src/
# it is vendoring rather than pick up whatever a developer happened to have on disk: a stale dist/
# riding along is a workspace whose JS and whose sources disagree, in an image, silently.
**/node_modules
dist
.git
coverage
